algorithms.pseudocode:
function BERGGREN_TREE(a, b, c, D):
    result <- [(e, (a,b,c), 0)]
    if D > 0:
        for (label, gen) in [(A, bergA), (B, bergB), (C, bergC)]:
            (a'', b'', c'') <- gen(a, b, c)
            result <- result U BERGGREN_TREE(a'', b'', c'', D-1)
    return result

Complexity: O(3^D) nodes, O(1) per node.
